    "title": "Ford ended an 11-year career over a $1.95 cookie - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Gesi Lloyd ,\n8 hours ago Kurt Kromm spent 11 years working at Ford’s Kentucky Truck Plant in Louisville, a factory that builds the Super Duty, the Expedition and the Lincoln Navigator. That career came to an abrupt end in May over an accusation that he failed to pay for a $1.95 chocolate chip cookie, a claim Kromm says was flatly untrue and one he eventually proved with his own bank statement. Read full article",
